Remove existing Software Deployment:

1. Under the existing SentinelOne GPO, navigate to:
   Computer Configuration > Policies > Software Settings > Software Installation
2. Right-click the package, then under "All Tasks" select "Remove...".
3. On the popup, select:
   "Allow users to continue to use the software, but prevent new installations"




Copy files to NETLOGON

Copy Install-SentinelOne.ps1 and the SentinelOne installer MSI to:
   \\DOMAIN.TLD\NETLOGON\S1\




Scheduled Task (Preferred)

1. Under the existing SentinelOne GPO, navigate to:
   Computer Configuration > Preferences > Control Panel Settings > Scheduled Tasks

2. In the empty right-hand pane, right-click and select:
   New > Scheduled Task (At least Windows 7)

3. Under the "General" tab:
   - Set the name to "Tenax S1 Deploy"
   - Set the user running the task to "SYSTEM"
   - Select "Run whether user is logged on or not"
   - Check "Run with highest privileges"
   - Set "Configure for" to Windows 7 or newer

4. Under the "Triggers" tab:
   - Set the task to run on a daily schedule
   - Set "Recur every" to 1 day
   - Set "Delay task for up to (random delay)" to 1 minute
   - Ensure "Enabled" is checked

5. Under the "Actions" tab:
   - Set the action type to "Start a program"
   - Set the program/script to:
     powershell.exe
   - Set the arguments to (replace DOMAIN.TLD, <VERSION> and S1_TOKEN):
     -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "\\DOMAIN.TLD\NETLOGON\S1\Install-SentinelOne.ps1" -InstallerPath "\\DOMAIN.TLD\NETLOGON\S1\SentinelInstaller_windows_64bit_v<VERSION>.msi" -SiteToken "S1_TOKEN"

6. Under the "Conditions" tab:
   - Uncheck "Start the task only if the computer is on AC power"
   - Uncheck "Stop if the computer switches to battery power"

7. Under the "Settings" tab:
   - Set "Stop the task if it runs longer than" to 1 hour




Import GPO from Zip file (alternative to building the task by hand)

1. Extract SentinelOne-ScheduledTask.zip to C:\backup
   (C:\backup should contain manifest.xml and the {C452D176-...} folder).

2. Import it:
   Import-GPO -BackupId "C452D176-8E49-410C-9AB7-3764442F6B2D" -Path "C:\backup" -TargetName "SentinelOne" -CreateIfNeeded

3. Edit the imported "Tenax S1 Deploy" task (Actions tab) and replace the placeholders:
   - DOMAIN.TLD -> your domain (e.g. contoso.local)
   - S1_TOKEN   -> the site token from the SentinelOne console
   The installer file name in the task is for v26.2.3.158; update it if you use a different version.

4. Link the GPO to the OUs that should get SentinelOne.
